# 🔴 ADDED 2026-08-26, BEFORE the repo goes public. Neither pattern existed, and the repository has
# never held a secret (criterion 10.7's sweep: 506 commits, zero named-format hits) — which is
# exactly why the rules were missing and exactly why they have to exist NOW. A `.gitignore` that has
# never been tested by a real `.env` is not evidence that one would be caught.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Vercel's project link and pulled environment. `.vercel/` carries the project + org ids and,
# after `vercel env pull`, real values.
.vercel/
# Appended by `vercel link` on 2026-08-27. Redundant with the rules above — kept because they are
# what the CLI re-adds if removed, and a rule fighting the tool is a rule that loses quietly.
.vercel
.env*

# The mutation runner writes its vitest report here. Never committed.
_mutation-vt.json
